1
00:00:00,300 --> 00:00:02,480
ActionGate, check that action.

2
00:00:04,660 --> 00:00:06,900
Before the agent takes a step.

3
00:00:09,180 --> 00:00:11,910
A supplier document, deadlines and details.

4
00:00:11,940 --> 00:00:13,930
An embedded command tries to change our
rules.

5
00:00:14,273 --> 00:00:16,913
ActionGate checks that action before it
runs.

6
00:00:17,106 --> 00:00:20,779
It connects agents to models, APIs and MCP
services

7
00:00:20,926 --> 00:00:23,937
through a gateway that enforces the
organization's rules.

8
00:00:24,595 --> 00:00:28,337
Here is a real supplier review using
synthetic business data.

9
00:00:28,995 --> 00:00:31,796
We start the interactive checks in the
dashboard.

10
00:00:32,350 --> 00:00:35,419
The agent reads its approved document
through MCP,

11
00:00:35,531 --> 00:00:38,089
asks the local business model for a summary,

12
00:00:38,201 --> 00:00:41,363
saves protected memory and creates an
internal report.

13
00:00:41,916 --> 00:00:44,184
Open the document operation and you can see

14
00:00:44,204 --> 00:00:47,667
the actual connector receipt alongside the
decision.

15
00:00:48,128 --> 00:00:50,384
Now compare three other outcomes.

16
00:00:50,844 --> 00:00:53,762
Personal data is redacted before the report
is saved.

17
00:00:54,014 --> 00:00:56,142
An instruction that tries to redirect

18
00:00:56,162 --> 00:00:58,813
the workflow is blocked before dispatch.

19
00:00:59,181 --> 00:01:03,596
And a request for another tenant's document
is rejected by access policy.

20
00:01:04,057 --> 00:01:08,937
That access boundary remains in force
independently of the semantic model.

21
00:01:09,188 --> 00:01:11,421
The same controls follow the workflow.

22
00:01:11,882 --> 00:01:15,032
Reading confidential information restricts
later actions,

23
00:01:15,145 --> 00:01:17,563
including delegated work and memory.

24
00:01:18,221 --> 00:01:20,674
Publishing a protected report requires
approval of

25
00:01:20,694 --> 00:01:23,705
its exact content and permitted recipient.

26
00:01:24,502 --> 00:01:27,176
Operators manage a signed control catalog.

27
00:01:27,486 --> 00:01:30,485
Change the profile, adjust a threshold or
publish

28
00:01:30,505 --> 00:01:34,003
a threat rule, then inspect the active
generation.

29
00:01:34,557 --> 00:01:36,488
Strict can block personal data.

30
00:01:36,856 --> 00:01:38,473
Balanced can redact it.

31
00:01:39,027 --> 00:01:41,271
Policy comparison shows how a candidate

32
00:01:41,291 --> 00:01:44,685
changes decisions without repeating business
effects.

33
00:01:47,700 --> 00:01:49,730
Tokens, model time, external call costs.

34
00:01:49,760 --> 00:01:51,910
Limits are checked before actions incur
costs.

35
00:01:51,940 --> 00:01:54,070
Delegated work still shares one budget.

36
00:01:54,100 --> 00:01:56,510
Scoped views. A reason for every decision.

37
00:01:56,540 --> 00:01:58,550
Change a rule and compare its effects.

38
00:01:58,580 --> 00:02:01,400
No repeated actions. No guessing the
difference.

39
00:02:05,047 --> 00:02:06,014
Change a rule.

40
00:02:06,266 --> 00:02:07,593
Try your own input.

41
00:02:07,961 --> 00:02:09,497
Follow the resulting action.

42
00:02:09,540 --> 00:02:12,086
ActionGate gives teams the controls and
evidence

43
00:02:12,106 --> 00:02:14,141
to put useful agents to work.
